                "text": ", ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "cfg.MaxAckPending = cap(ch)",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "). ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "jsconsumer",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " sends the field on every start, so leaving it zero would have rewritten all seven durables to the server default silently. Setting 1000 makes it a recorded decision instead. Either number is generous at a one-message prefetch — in-flight work is one delivery per replica.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
