          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "What does not move",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "Give-up semantics.",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " No Term path, no ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "Retry",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": ", no DLQ. The event is republished verbatim, so nothing about it can be permanently unprocessable; and ",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "text": "resource_lifecycle_v1",
                "type": "text",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "code"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": " is limits-retention, holding every event for its full max age whatever this consumer does — so the replay path is the source stream, not a capture stream. Adding capture would need a DLQ stream ",
                "type": "text"
